# Analysis

The issue is that when you select a child chat or navigate to the parent, the `targetProject` is not being updated to reflect the selected chat's project. The `ProjectDetailt` selector is bound to `targetProject`, but it's only set during `init()` based on `theChat.project_id`.

When you call `selectChildChat(childChat)`, you change `showChildChat`, which updates the `workingChat` computed property, but `targetProject` remains unchanged.

## Solution

Add a watcher to update `targetProject` whenever `workingChat` changes:

```vue client/src/views/ChatView.vue
<script>
export default {
  // ... existing code ...

  watch: {
    chat(newVal, oldVal) {
      if (oldVal && newVal && oldVal.project_id !== newVal.project_id) {
        this.init()
      }
      this.showChildChat = null
      this.showHistoryWall = false
    },
    // Add this watcher to update targetProject when workingChat changes
    workingChat(newVal) {
      if (newVal) {
        this.targetProject = this.$projects.allProjectsById[newVal.project_id] || this.$project
        this.subtaskProject = this.targetProject
      }
    }
  },

  // ... rest of the code ...
}
</script>
```

This watcher ensures that whenever the `workingChat` changes (either by selecting a child chat or navigating to the parent), the `targetProject` selector will automatically update to reflect the current chat's project.

The watcher will trigger:
- When `selectChildChat(childChat)` is called
- When `navigateToParent(parentChat)` is called
- When switching between parent and child chats
